        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Robinson, Jr.; Thomas Graves; Charles I of England\n- Places: Charlestown; Boston; Massachusetts; United States\n- Roles: mayor; engineer\n\nFacts:\n- In 1629, Charlestown was laid out by engineer Thomas Graves, one of its early settlers, during the reign of Charles I of England.\n- Charlestown is the oldest neighborhood in Boston, Massachusetts, United States.\n- Charles Robinson, Jr. was born on November 6, 1829.\n- Charles Robinson, Jr. served as the eighth mayor of Charlestown, Massachusetts.\n- Charles Robinson, Jr. died on July 30, 1891.",
